<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Literary Science</title>
<meta name="description" content="Literature from marginalized communities is operational technology. It renders designed systems visible. Literary Science puts what writers have seen to work — in classrooms, on campuses, in communities.">
<link rel="canonical" href="https://literaryscience.com">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
<style>
  .hero {
    min-height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    padding: 8rem 3rem 5rem;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    position: relative;
  }

  .hero-title {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 7.5rem);
    line-height: 0.95;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    opacity: 0;
    animation: revealSlow 1.5s cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.1, 0.25, 1) 0.1s forwards;
  }

  .hero-title .line-2 {
    display: block;
    opacity: 0;
    animation: revealSlow 1.5s cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.1, 0.25, 1) 0.3s forwards;
  }

  .hero-sub {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faded);
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    opacity: 0;
    animation: fadeIn 1.5s ease 0.8s forwards;
  }

  .hero-rule {
    width: 50px; height: 1px;
    background: var(--faded);
    margin-top: 2rem;
    opacity: 0;
    animation: expandLine 1.2s ease 1.1s forwards;
  }

  .hero-description {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    max-width: 560px;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    opacity: 0;
    animation: fadeIn 1.5s ease 1.3s forwards;
  }

  .hero-scroll {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 2.5rem; left: 3rem;
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.5rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--paper-dark);
    writing-mode: vertical-rl;
    opacity: 0;
    animation: fadeIn 1.5s ease 2s forwards;
  }

  /* marquee */
  .marquee {
    padding: 0.7rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .marquee-track {
    display: flex; width: max-content;
    animation: scroll 60s linear infinite;
  }
  .marquee-item {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 0.85rem; font-style: italic;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em; white-space: nowrap;
    padding: 0 2rem; color: var(--faded); opacity: 0.6;
  }
  .marquee-dot { padding: 0 0.5rem; color: var(--paper-dark); }

  /* four movements */
  .movements-section {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 5rem 3rem 2rem;
  }

  .movements-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .movements-label {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.5rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faded);
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  }

  .movements-title {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    max-width: 600px;
  }

  .movements-intro {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    max-width: 560px;
    margin-top: 1.2rem;
  }

  .movements-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
  }

  .movement {
    padding: 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
    border-right: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
    transition: transform 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.1, 0.25, 1), box-shadow 0.4s ease, background 0.4s ease;
    cursor: default;
  }

  .movement:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    background: var(--paper-light);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);
  }

  .movement:nth-child(2n) { border-right: none; }

  .movement-num {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-size: 3rem; font-weight: 700;
    opacity: 0.05; line-height: 1; margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }

  .movement-name {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .movement-question {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--faded);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .movement-desc {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    max-width: 420px;
  }

  /* quote */
  .home-quote {
    padding: 4.5rem 3rem;
    background: var(--ink);
    text-align: center;
    position: relative; overflow: hidden;
  }
  .home-quote::before, .home-quote::after {
    content: ''; position: absolute;
    top: 0; bottom: 0; width: 20px;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom,
      transparent 0px, transparent 3px,
      rgba(242,242,242,0.03) 3px, rgba(242,242,242,0.03) 4px);
  }
  .home-quote::before { left: 0; }
  .home-quote::after { right: 0; }
  .home-quote blockquote {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2.5vw, 1.6rem);
    font-style: italic; line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; color: var(--paper);
  }
  .home-quote cite {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300; font-size: 0.48rem; font-style: normal;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase;
    display: block; margin-top: 1.5rem; color: var(--faded);
  }

  /* zone grid */
  .zones {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .zone {
    padding: 4rem 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
    border-right: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
    transition: background 0.5s;
    text-decoration: none; color: var(--ink);
    display: block;
  }
  .zone:nth-child(2n) { border-right: none; }
  .zone:hover { background: var(--paper-light); }

  .zone-num {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-size: 4rem; font-weight: 700;
    opacity: 0.04; line-height: 1; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .zone-title {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.5rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .zone-subtitle {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300; font-size: 0.5rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faded); margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }
  .zone-desc {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--warm-gray); max-width: 420px;
  }
  .zone-arrow {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300; font-size: 0.55rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--paper-dark); margin-top: 1.5rem; display: block;
    transition: color 0.3s;
  }
  .zone:hover .zone-arrow { color: var(--ink); }

  /* full-width zone */
  .zone-full {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    border-right: none;
  }
  .zone-full:hover { background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); }
  .zone-full:hover .zone-desc { color: var(--paper-dark); }
  .zone-full:hover .zone-subtitle { color: var(--faded); }
  .zone-full:hover .zone-arrow { color: var(--paper); }

  .zone-full-left { padding-right: 2rem; }
  .zone-full-right {
    padding-left: 2rem;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: flex-end;
  }
  .zone-full:hover .zone-full-right { border-left-color: rgba(242,242,242,0.1); }

  .zone-stat { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .stat-number {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-size: 2.8rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1;
  }
  .stat-label {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300; font-size: 0.48rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faded); margin-top: 0.2rem;
  }

  /* workshops strip */
  .workshops-strip {
    padding: 4rem 3rem;
    background: var(--ink);
    text-align: center;
    position: relative; overflow: hidden;
  }
  .workshops-strip::before, .workshops-strip::after {
    content: ''; position: absolute;
    top: 0; bottom: 0; width: 20px;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom,
      transparent 0px, transparent 3px,
      rgba(242,242,242,0.03) 3px, rgba(242,242,242,0.03) 4px);
  }
  .workshops-strip::before { left: 0; }
  .workshops-strip::after { right: 0; }
  .workshops-strip h2 {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.8rem;
    color: var(--paper); margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .workshops-strip p {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--paper-dark);
    max-width: 480px; margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .workshops-strip a {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300; font-size: 0.55rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none; color: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
    padding: 0.7rem 1.6rem;
    display: inline-block; margin-top: 2rem;
    transition: all 0.3s;
  }
  .workshops-strip a:hover {
    background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .hero { padding: 7rem 1.5rem 3rem; }
    .movements-section { padding: 3rem 1.5rem 1rem; }
    .movements-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .movement { border-right: none; padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem; }
    .zones { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .zone { border-right: none; padding: 3rem 1.5rem; }
    .zone-full { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .zone-full-right {
      border-left: none; padding-left: 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
      padding-top: 2rem; margin-top: 2rem;
    }
    .zone-full:hover .zone-full-right { border-top-color: rgba(242,242,242,0.1); }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<nav>
  <a href="/" class="nav-logo">Literary Science</a>
  <ul class="nav-links">
    <li><a href="/epistemology/">Methodology</a></li>
    <li><a href="/toolkit/">Toolkit</a></li>
    <li><a href="/studio/">Studio</a></li>
    <li><a href="/newcomm/">NewComm</a></li>
    <li><a href="/workshops/">Workshops</a></li>
  </ul>
</nav>

<section class="hero">
  <h1 class="hero-title">Literary<span class="line-2">Science.</span></h1>
  <div class="hero-sub">What we have read &mdash; How we investigate it in the world</div>
  <div class="hero-rule"></div>
  <p class="hero-description">Literature from marginalized communities is operational technology. It renders designed systems visible. Literary Science puts what writers have seen to work&mdash;in classrooms, on campuses, in communities.</p>
  <div class="hero-scroll">Scroll &darr;</div>
</section>

<div class="marquee">
  <div class="marquee-track">
    <span class="marquee-item">&ldquo;Not everything that is faced can be changed, but nothing can be changed until it is faced.&rdquo; &mdash; James Baldwin</span><span class="marquee-dot">&bull;</span>
    <span class="marquee-item">&ldquo;All that you touch you change. All that you change changes you.&rdquo; &mdash; Octavia Butler</span><span class="marquee-dot">&bull;</span>
    <span class="marquee-item">&ldquo;If there&rsquo;s a book you want to read, but it hasn&rsquo;t been written yet, then you must write it.&rdquo; &mdash; Toni Morrison</span><span class="marquee-dot">&bull;</span>
    <span class="marquee-item">&ldquo;Stories matter. Many stories matter.&rdquo; &mdash; Chimamanda Ngozi Adichie</span><span class="marquee-dot">&bull;</span>
    <span class="marquee-item">&ldquo;What is most important to me must be spoken, made verbal and shared.&rdquo; &mdash; Audre Lorde</span><span class="marquee-dot">&bull;</span>
    <span class="marquee-item">&ldquo;To be truly visionary we have to root our imagination in our concrete reality while simultaneously imagining possibilities beyond that reality.&rdquo; &mdash; bell hooks</span><span class="marquee-dot">&bull;</span>
    <span class="marquee-item">&ldquo;Not everything that is faced can be changed, but nothing can be changed until it is faced.&rdquo; &mdash; James Baldwin</span><span class="marquee-dot">&bull;</span>
    <span class="marquee-item">&ldquo;All that you touch you change. All that you change changes you.&rdquo; &mdash; Octavia Butler</span><span class="marquee-dot">&bull;</span>
    <span class="marquee-item">&ldquo;If there&rsquo;s a book you want to read, but it hasn&rsquo;t been written yet, then you must write it.&rdquo; &mdash; Toni Morrison</span><span class="marquee-dot">&bull;</span>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="movements-section reveal">
  <div class="movements-header">
    <div class="movements-label">The Framework</div>
    <h2 class="movements-title">Four Movements</h2>
    <p class="movements-intro">Literary Science operates through four sequential movements. Each builds on the one before it. Together they form a complete arc from observation to action&mdash;from reading a novel to building something that interrupts the design.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="movements-grid" style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto;">
  <div class="movement reveal">
    <div class="movement-num">01</div>
    <div class="movement-name">Asset Mapping</div>
    <div class="movement-question">Who has what?</div>
    <p class="movement-desc">Identify the resources, relationships, and power inside the text&mdash;and inside the community. See what exists before diagnosing what&rsquo;s missing.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="movement reveal" style="transition-delay: 0.08s;">
    <div class="movement-num">02</div>
    <div class="movement-name">Flow Analysis</div>
    <div class="movement-question">How do things move?</div>
    <p class="movement-desc">Track how information, trust, and capital circulate&mdash;or get stuck. The system&rsquo;s assets are not the problem. The problem is how they move.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="movement reveal">
    <div class="movement-num">03</div>
    <div class="movement-name">Strategic Response</div>
    <div class="movement-question">What do you do with what you see?</div>
    <p class="movement-desc">Convert observations into decisions. Asset Mapping and Flow Analysis produce understanding. Strategic Response produces action.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="movement reveal" style="transition-delay: 0.08s;">
    <div class="movement-num">04</div>
    <div class="movement-name">Creative Restoration</div>
    <div class="movement-question">How do you rebuild?</div>
    <p class="movement-desc">Design new structures that are more honest, more durable, more human. Restore what the community should have had in the first place.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="home-quote reveal">
  <blockquote>&ldquo;The novel is not studied. It is used. The project that emerges is not inspired by the book. It is built from it.&rdquo;</blockquote>
  <cite>Literary Science</cite>
</div>

<div class="zones">
  <a href="/epistemology/" class="zone reveal">
    <div class="zone-num">01</div>
    <div class="zone-title">The Methodology</div>
    <div class="zone-subtitle">Why Literature Is Technology</div>
    <p class="zone-desc">The intellectual architecture. Why literature from marginalized communities functions as operational technology. How a novel becomes a response to a designed system.</p>
    <span class="zone-arrow">Read the methodology &rarr;</span>
  </a>

  <a href="/toolkit/" class="zone reveal" style="transition-delay: 0.08s;">
    <div class="zone-num">02</div>
    <div class="zone-title">The Toolkit</div>
    <div class="zone-subtitle">Free Tools &amp; Reading List</div>
    <p class="zone-desc">The open shelf by the door. One-pagers, classroom protocols, hypothesis templates, reading list. Things a teacher downloads Friday and uses Monday morning. No gate.</p>
    <span class="zone-arrow">Browse the tools &rarr;</span>
  </a>

  <a href="/studio/" class="zone reveal">
    <div class="zone-num">03</div>
    <div class="zone-title">The Studio</div>
    <div class="zone-subtitle">Musings, Drawings &amp; Asides</div>
    <p class="zone-desc">The table covered in open books and sketches. Connections between Killer of Sheep and housing policy. A drawing pinned next to a paragraph from Toni Morrison. The thinking before it becomes formal.</p>
    <span class="zone-arrow">Enter the studio &rarr;</span>
  </a>

  <a href="/newcomm/" class="zone zone-full reveal">
    <div class="zone-full-left">
      <div class="zone-num">04</div>
      <div class="zone-title">NewComm</div>
      <div class="zone-subtitle">Literary Science at Full Scale</div>
      <p class="zone-desc">What happens when Literary Science transforms what a campus is for. NewComm operates at independent schools&mdash;Horace Mann, Poly Prep&mdash;places with extraordinary assets that can serve a larger purpose. The infrastructure, the networks, the credibility. All of it activated for work that benefits everyone in the building and everyone beyond the gate.</p>
      <span class="zone-arrow">See it in practice &rarr;</span>
    </div>
    <div class="zone-full-right">
      <div class="zone-stat">
        <div class="stat-number">$10K</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Per Company &mdash; real capital into marginalized communities</div>
      </div>
      <div class="zone-stat">
        <div class="stat-number">5</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Week Summer Intensive</div>
      </div>
      <div class="zone-stat">
        <div class="stat-number">12</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Month Loop &mdash; experimentation to execution</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </a>
</div>

<div class="workshops-strip reveal">
  <h2>Bring this to your space.</h2>
  <p>Literary Science runs in-person workshops for schools, museums, libraries, and community organizations. If you want this methodology in your context, let&rsquo;s talk.</p>
  <a href="/workshops/">Learn more &rarr;</a>
</div>

<footer>
  <div class="footer-left">Literary Science</div>
  <div class="footer-right">A property of Asoluka LLC &nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp; <a href="/workshops/">Contact</a> &nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp; &copy; 2026</div>
</footer>

<script>
  const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
    entries.forEach(e => { if (e.isIntersecting) e.target.classList.add('visible'); });
  }, { threshold: 0.1 });
  document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(el => observer.observe(el));
</script>
</body>
</html>
